          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em relative entropy
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state"} states
            is a generalization of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entropy"} entropy
            to a situation where the entropy of one
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state"} state
            is measured “relative to” another state.
          %p It is also called
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em> Kullback-Leibler divergence
                ,
            %li
              %p
                %em> information divergence
                , or
            %li
              %p
                %em> information gain
                \.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#OnFiniteDimensionalSpaces For states on finite probability spaces
          %p
            For two finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+distributions"} probability distributions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p_i)
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi q
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (q_i)
            %strong relative entropy
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi log
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi k
                  %mo −
                  %mi log
                  %msub
                    %mi q
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S(p/q) := \sum_{k = 1}^n p_k(log p_k - log q_k)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Alternatively, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho, \phi
            two
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/density+matrix"} density matrices
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi tr
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi log
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo −
                  %mi log
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S(\rho/\phi) := tr \rho(log \rho - log \phi)
                  \\,.
          %h3#for_states_on_classical_probability_spaces For states on classical probability spaces
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+space"} measurable space
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+measure"} probability measures
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              is absolutely continuous with respect to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral"} integral
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi X
                    %mi log
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mi Q
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mi P
                    %mi d
                    %mi P
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S(Q|P) = \int_X log \frac{d Q}{d P} d P
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi d
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d Q / d P
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Radon-Nikodym+derivative"} Radon-Nikodym derivative
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              with respect to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
          %h3#for_states_on_quantum_probability_spaces_von_neumann_algebras For states on quantum probability spaces (von Neumann algebras)
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/von+Neumann+algebra"} von Neumann algebra
            and let
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi : A \to \mathbb{C}
            be two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state"} states
            on it (faithful, positive
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+functional"} linear functionals
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong
                relative entropy
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(\phi/\psi)
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ψ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
                relative to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ψ
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi log
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mrow
                        %mi Φ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S(\phi/\psi) := - (\Psi, (log \Delta_{\Phi,\Psi}) \Psi)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mrow
                        %mi Φ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_{\Phi,\Psi}
              is the relative
              %span.newWikiWord
                modular operator
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/modular+operator"} ?
              of any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+vector"} cyclic
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separating+vector"} separating vector
              representatives
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ψ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
          %p
            This is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Araki"}> Araki
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %ul
              %li
                %p This definition is independent of the choice of these representatives.
              %li
                %p
                  In the case that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  is finite dimensional and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ρ
                          %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho_\phi
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ρ
                          %mi ψ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho_\psi
                  are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/density+matrices"} density matrices
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                  and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ψ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "#OnFiniteDimensionalSpaces"} above definition
          %h2#relation_to_machine_learning Relation to machine learning
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/machine+learning"} machine learning
            process has been characterized as a minimization of relative entropy (
            %a{:href => "#AckleyHintonSejnowski"}> Ackley, Hinton and Sejnowski 1985
            ).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fisher+metric"} Fisher metric
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/information+geometry"} information geometry
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/machine+learning"} machine learning
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Relative entropy of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state+on+a+star-algebra"} states
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/von+Neumann+algebras"} von Neumann algebras
            was introduced in:
          %ul
            %li#Araki
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Huzihiro+Araki"}> Huzihiro Araki
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Relative Entropy of States of von Neumann Algebras
              %strong 11
              3 (1976), 809-833 (
              %a{:href => "https://ems.press/content/serial-article-files/2833"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2977/prims/1195191148"} doi:10.2977/prims/1195191148
          %p
            A characterization of
            %a{:href => "#OnFiniteDimensionalSpaces"} relative entropy
            on finite-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-star+algebra"} C-star algebras
            is given in
          %ul
            %li#Petz
              D. Petz,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Characterization of the relative entropy of states of matrix algebras
              %strong 59
              (1992), 3-4. (
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/bf00050907"}> doi:10.1007/bf00050907
              )
          %p
            A survey of entropy in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+algebra"} operator algebras
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              Erling Størmer,
              %em Entropy in operator algebras
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.claymath.org/publications/currentvolumes/connes60/Stormer.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            A characterization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/machine+learning"} machine learning
            as a process minimizing relative entropy is proposed in
          %ul
            %li#AckleyHintonSejnowski
              David H. Ackley, Geoffrey E. Hilton, Terrence J. Sejnowski.
              = succeed "," do
                %em A learning algorithm for Boltzmann machines
              %strong 9
              (1985), 147–169. (
              %a{:href => "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0364021385800124"}> web
              )
